">I totally agree with both points.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a note, I did think that Misery should have been more overtly Monica Black but is kinda just, &quot;90% Monica black.&quot;<br /> <br /> I do love the Vancouver tie-in, though.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T15:47:12-07:00","id":1449393,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: I read the Vancouver book a while ago cause someone I knew had it in physical form and while most of it was forgettable (or at least I forgot it), I did think Prince Siegfried would\u2019ve been a better Brujah than a Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T01:07:04-07:00","id":1449436,"title":"","content":"The loresheets are neat. I especially like The One True Way. Don't much care for the Rancho - being tied to a set location, it'll probably never feature in any of my games. And I'm pretty tired of the Hecata loresheets. They are already the single most covered clan in the game, give some love to the others.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of the sample cult coterie being the people who explicitly think their cult is bullshit and they are just there to make a buck. Unless the sentiment there is that the average vampire cult <i>is</i> all just vampires pulling a con, but that doesn't really jive with the rest of the book.<br /> <br /> I'm also kinda iffy of the &quot;refined&quot; Influence (Church) since most things split into those individual points are things I'd already expect to do by just rolling Influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T01:29:49-07:00","id":1449437,"title":"","content":"<br /> In my opinion, it is not an essential book, but it is interesting. In general, all the characters are well developed, and written in deep, with many hooks to be introduced in your chronicles. On the contrary of Children of the Inquisition, they are not elders that are going to steal the spotlight, and they are not Princes, Justicars and political power players, as most of the characters in Children of the Night. They are believers, priests, sectarians and any kind of people that have ended being entangled by the webs of faith. Vampires can have superpowers, but they are as vulnerable as humans to manipulation and desperation, they need something to believe in.<br /> <br /> Of the 27 characters, two are old characters from Milwaukee by night (Akawa and Anastasia), the other are brand new! I enjoyed these six the most: Faith Corrigan, Roberto Vega, Morawitz, Miss Fitzsimmons, Euan Dunsirn and Mari Jane Hollingsworth. There are some links to former chronicles and there are some characters that are going to make an appearance in Tail of bone and ashes, for sure. But even more interesting, there are two character (Roberto Vega and Dr. Starr) that make references to Boston and will have some impact in Vampire The Masquerade Swansong, an incoming videogame that has been scripted by Gentleman gamer.<br /> <br /> There was only one character which I do not liked it, the Ventrue named Von Kral, it seemed to me too archetypical. But I can deal with that, it is not one of the more important character, I guess. I also noted that there is other chinese character that it is not a Kuei-jin, so other nail in the coffin of the polemic Kindred of the east. There are many clues that point that they are not going to come back.<br /> <br /> The additional rules for coteries, merits and flaws are fine, but even more optional. Finally, the loresheets, they have include two more Hecata bloodlines (they rise to 10, now) and some sheets for cults. I am interested in the One true way, if I remember correctly it is mentioned both in Lair of the hidden and the Beckett Diary, being a plot of an Inconnu elder to destroy other aspirants or researchers of the Golconda. Finally, the author have find an interesting way to the introduce the Inconnu in the street-level chronicles.<br /> <br /> 4/5 stars.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have wrote a review in spanish here:<br /> Part 1 <a href=\"https://webvampiro.com/foro/viewtopic.php?f=15&amp;t=2590&amp;p=57133#p57133\" target=\"_blank\">https://webvampiro.com/foro/viewtopi...p=57133#p57133</a><br /> Part 2 <a href=\"https://webvampiro.com/foro/viewtopic.php?f=15&amp;t=2590&amp;start=30#p57136\" target=\"_blank\">https://webvampiro.com/foro/viewtopi...tart=30#p57136</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 05-24-2021, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T01:52:30-07:00","id":1449438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449379-what-do-you-guys-think-of-children-of-the-blood?p=1449384#post1449384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely love this book and am glad to have contributed some character 